            ("Symbolism", "The literary use of an object, person, situation, or color to represent an abstract meaning or conceptual reality beyond its literal identity", "An exact literal representation", "A comic physical gesture", "A grammatical modifier clause"),
            ("Foreshadowing", "The author's deliberate placement of subtle clues, hints, or omens early in the narrative suggesting future events or disastrous outcomes", "Recalling memories from youth", "Interrupting with authorial intrusion", "Resolving the final conflict"),
            ("Analepsis (Flashback)", "A narrative interruption that shifts the scene backward in time to depict events that transpired prior to the current narrative moment", "Leaping forward to future years", "Direct conversation with audience", "A monologue delivered alone"),
