            ("Negritude Movement (Aime Cesaire, Leopold Senghor)", "Literary and ideological movement affirming Black cultural identity, pan-African dignity, and pride against French colonial assimilation", "Rejection of traditional African values", "Adoption of European cultural supremacy", "A military guerilla alliance"),
