            ("Arena Stage (Theatre-in-the-Round)", "A performance space completely encircled by the audience on all four sides, demanding multi-directional actor blocking", "A stage with an arch frame", "A platform with no audience", "A high balcony platform"),
            ("Catharsis (in Poetics)", "Aristotle's concept of the purgation, cleansing, and emotional purification of pity and fear produced by the climax of a tragic catastrophe", "A burst of vulgar laughter", "A demand for financial refund", "A political demonstration on stage"),
